{%- comment -%}
  Data-only section for the Member setup notice (snippets/at-member-setup.liquid →
  assets/at-member-setup.js). Not placed in any template. Fetched while a signed-in customer's
  session has no B2B company location yet:
    /?sections=at-member-setup-data

  Wagner sets up a new account a few seconds after sign-up (company, Member location, then the
  `wagner.tier` customer metafield). Until the session buys for that location, the page shows
  guest prices. This reports, from Shopify only (never Wagner):
  - tier: the `wagner.tier` customer metafield ('' until Wagner writes it).
  - b2b: the session is buying for a company location, so catalog prices apply.
  - setLocationUrl: Shopify's URL that makes the customer's tier location current without
    signing out (`location.url_to_set_as_current`), or '' when there is none yet. The location
    named after the tier wins; otherwise the first available one.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign at_tier = ''
  assign at_b2b = false
  assign at_set_url = ''
  if customer
    assign at_tier = customer.metafields.wagner.tier.value | default: '' | downcase | strip
    if customer.b2b? and customer.current_location
      assign at_b2b = true
    endif
    unless at_b2b
      for location in customer.company_available_locations
        assign at_loc_name = location.name | downcase
        if at_set_url == ''
          assign at_set_url = location.url_to_set_as_current
        endif
        if at_tier != '' and at_loc_name contains at_tier
          assign at_set_url = location.url_to_set_as_current
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endunless
  endif
-%}
<script type="application/json" data-at-member-setup>
  {"signedIn":{% if customer %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},"tier":{{ at_tier | json }},"b2b":{{ at_b2b }},"setLocationUrl":{{ at_set_url | json }}}
</script>
